{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c856c6276987e2b4","name":"card_unit_30_infantry_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_30_infantry_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"30. INFANTRY REGIMENT","text":"Reduce operation cost by 1 after you operate a German unit.","flavorText":"The 30th Infantry Regiment was part of the 18th Infantry Division, a formation whose wartime service stretched from the opening campaigns of 1939 to the final battle in Berlin. Mobilized in August 1939, the 18th Infantry Division took part in the invasion of Poland before fighting in the Battle of France in 1940. Following the French campaign, the division was motorized and redesignated the 18th Motorized Infantry Division. From June 1941 it fought on the Eastern Front, first in the central sector and later in the North. In June 1943, the formation became the 18th Panzergrenadier Division. It continued fighting on the Eastern Front but was devastated during the Soviet summer offensive of 1944. Its surviving members later fought in East Prussia and ultimately in the Battle of Berlin. When Berlin surrendered on 2 May 1945, they attempted to fight their way out of the encircled city.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":4,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_30_infantry_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_30_infantry_regiment_title","SourceString":"30. INFANTRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"30. INFANTRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_30_infantry_regiment_text","SourceString":"Reduce operation cost by 1 after you operate a German unit.","LocalizedString":"Reduce operation cost by 1 after you operate a German unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_30_infantry_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 30th Infantry Regiment was part of the 18th Infantry Division, a formation whose wartime service stretched from the opening campaigns of 1939 to the final battle in Berlin. Mobilized in August 1939, the 18th Infantry Division took part in the invasion of Poland before fighting in the Battle of France in 1940. Following the French campaign, the division was motorized and redesignated the 18th Motorized Infantry Division. From June 1941 it fought on the Eastern Front, first in the central sector and later in the North. In June 1943, the formation became the 18th Panzergrenadier Division. It continued fighting on the Eastern Front but was devastated during the Soviet summer offensive of 1944. Its surviving members later fought in East Prussia and ultimately in the Battle of Berlin. When Berlin surrendered on 2 May 1945, they attempted to fight their way out of the encircled city.","LocalizedString":"The 30th Infantry Regiment was part of the 18th Infantry Division, a formation whose wartime service stretched from the opening campaigns of 1939 to the final battle in Berlin. Mobilized in August 1939, the 18th Infantry Division took part in the invasion of Poland before fighting in the Battle of France in 1940. Following the French campaign, the division was motorized and redesignated the 18th Motorized Infantry Division. From June 1941 it fought on the Eastern Front, first in the central sector and later in the North. In June 1943, the formation became the 18th Panzergrenadier Division. It continued fighting on the Eastern Front but was devastated during the Soviet summer offensive of 1944. Its surviving members later fought in East Prussia and ultimately in the Battle of Berlin. When Berlin surrendered on 2 May 1945, they attempted to fight their way out of the encircled city."},"operationCost":4,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ER